text:
I like a bit of music;
 I like a song of mine;
 To hear them over again,
 Is worth as much as wine!

The world was made in six days;
I don’t believe it; if it had been so,
I couldn’t have been made in five minutes.

We will not go inshore any more;
The sharks are very troublesome now;
I was just trying to get some sleep, when
They came with such an angry leap.

I will take no thought for food nor raiment;

In every place where I shall go, they are mine.

And another, from Thomas à Kempis' Imitation of Christ:

There's a magnet which will draw thee to me,
And the very thing thou dost desire;
I am thy heart and soul, my child, and free!
